<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n30748" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Nĕphĕlē</span></b> ,
			ēs, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>f</i>, = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Νεφέλη</span>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>The wife of Athamas, mother of Phrixus and
			Helle</i>, <i><span class="en">Hyg. Fab. 1</span></i>, sq.; cf. <i><span class="en">id.
				Astr. 2, 20</span></i>.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b> Derivv. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Nĕphĕlaeus</span></b> , a, um, <i>adj., Nephelæan</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pecus,</span>”
				i. e. <i>the ram that bore away Helle and Phrixus</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Val.
					Fl. 1, 56</span></i>
			. —</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Nĕphĕlēĭas</span></b> ,
				ădis, f., <i>the daughter of Nephele, Helle</i>, <i><span class="en">Luc. 9,
			956</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Nĕphĕ-lēis</span></b> ,
				ĭdos, f., <i>the daughter of Nephele, Helle</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 11,
				195</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>One of the companions of Diana</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 3,
				171</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
